compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Senseonics Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $485M market cap on $35M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +29% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -2596% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and -25% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $60M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -13.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 29% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 9.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-7.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 194% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 53/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Healthcare peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the